{"at": "2026-08-21T19:22:56.020734+00:00", "event_id": "01M0JWDEMM7VFVV8FCYZ34YTJF", "event_type": "DecisionPointOpened", "payload": {"actor_id": "cli", "actor_type": "human", "decision_point_id": "01M0JWDEMKXQ5CMAE9PFEK8GF9", "input_key": "stack_shape", "mission_id": "01M0JMK90CFFDKA4RCCTQK9675", "mission_slug": "retire-doctrine-term-01M0JMK9", "mission_type": "software-dev", "options": ["Per-wave: 6 active missions + deferred 4.0 removal (recommended)", "Coarser: ~3 grouped missions + deferred 4.0 removal", "Other"], "origin_flow": "plan", "origin_surface": "planning_interview", "phase": "PLAN", "question": "How should the stacked retirement plan be shaped? The spec prescribes ordering (canonical authority first, then executable CLI surfaces with 3.x aliases, then prose/docs/prompts) but not granularity. Evidence-grounded recommendation: one mission per surface wave \u2014 (1) guard wave 0, (2) glossary + charter-bundle authority rewrite, (3) CLI executable surfaces with hidden aliases, (4) packs source rename, (5) skills/agent artifacts, (6) docs prose \u2014 plus a 7th mission explicitly deferred to the 4.0 milestone (alias removal + zero-doctrine audit). Alternative: coarser grouping into ~3 missions. Which shape do you want?", "recorded_at": "2026-08-21T19:22:56.020734Z", "run_id": "01M0JWDEMKXQ5CMAE9PFEK8GF9", "state_entered_at": "2026-08-21T19:22:56.019764Z", "step_id": "plan.stack.shape"}}
